<1-0-2>{\selectlanguage {english}\color {blue}\bfseries \LRnum {2}--\LRnum {4}~}{\bfseries \selectlanguage {english}}{\selectlanguage {english}cf. YSv (PT, pp. 833): sukhasādhyaṃ lakṣayogam idānīṃ śṛṇu pārvati | pañcadhā lakṣayogaś ca ūrddhalakṣādibhedataḥ (\textit {ūrdhva} YK 2.1) || ūrddhalakṣam (\textit {ūrdhva} YK 2.2) adholakṣo (\textit {°lakṣaṃ} YK 2.2) bāhyalakṣaṃ (\textit {vāhya°} YK 2.2) tathaiva ca | madhyalakṣas (\textit {°lakṣaṃ} YK 2.2) tathā jñeyam antarlakṣas (\textit {°lakṣaṃ} YK 2.2) tathaiva ca |}</1-0-2>
<1-0-3>{\selectlanguage {english}\color {blue}\bfseries \LRnum {2}--\LRnum {4}~}{\bfseries \selectlanguage {english}}{\selectlanguage {english}cf. \citetitle {hathasamketacandrikajodhpur} (MMPP 2244, f.124r ll. 7–9): atha rājayogāṃgasukhasādhyo lakṣyayogaḥ kathyate || lakṣayogasya paṃcabhedāṃ bhavati | parā ūrdhvalakṣyāṃ bāhyalakṣyaṃ madhyalakṣyam antaralakṣyaṃ ceti |}</1-0-3>
